<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cutanda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1120</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cutanda was fought in June 1120 near Calamocha in Aragon, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-i-of-aragon">Alfonso I of Aragon</a>, aided by southern French lords, defeated an Almoravid army sent to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>. The victory secured his conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley and opened the way to the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calatayud">Calatayud</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daroca">Daroca</a>. It was one of the heaviest Almoravid defeats in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cutanda.jpg" alt="Battle of Cutanda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dv.uzzi · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cutanda.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
